  "subtitle": null,
  "byline": "Tyler Cowen",
  "publishedAt": "2026-08-22T06:37:48.000Z",
  "contentHtml": "<p>Yes I will be doing a Conversation with her.&nbsp; She has a new and very interesting book coming out, namely <span id=\"productTitle\"><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Time-Tax-Government-Wastes-Time_and/dp/0063442558/ref=sr_1_1?crid=26IUEBFINPWAD&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.uGgyyxuWDYCnWag8zsxby03x3dahrvRSsvd5tqmrOqNxcDGa2hQy8noqXU7_PgvaMU8wbSBzC-UwwbL_9QfEjw.hxtZSoVcZu6kWBSguc1PKR6R0e26GJXBGcriar141qE&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=annie%2Blowrey&amp;qid=1787333783&amp;sprefix=annie%2Blowrey%2Caps%2C159&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The Time Tax: How the Government Wastes Our Time―and How to Fix It</a>.&nbsp; More generally, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Annie_Lowrey\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">from Wikipedia</a>:</span></p>\n<blockquote><p>Annie M. Lowrey…is an American journalist who writes on politics and economic policy for&nbsp;<a id=\"mwFQ\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Atlantic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The Atlantic</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-PoliticoBlog_3-0\"></sup>&nbsp;Previously, Lowrey covered economic policy for&nbsp;<a id=\"mwGw\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The New York Times</a>&nbsp;and prior to that was the Moneybox columnist for&nbsp;<a id=\"mwHQ\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slate_(magazine)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Slate</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-4\"></sup>&nbsp;She was also a&nbsp;<a id=\"mwIg\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Staff_writer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">staff writer</a>&nbsp;for the&nbsp;<a id=\"mwJA\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_Independent\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Washington Independent</a>&nbsp;and was on the editorial staffs of&nbsp;<a id=\"mwJg\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foreign_Policy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Foreign Policy</a>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<a id=\"mwKA\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_Yorker\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The New Yorker</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-5\"></sup>&nbsp;She is a proponent of&nbsp;<a id=\"mwLQ\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Universal_basic_income\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">universal basic income</a>.</p></blockquote>\n<p>So what should I ask her?</p>",
